    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0435" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4000</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-22T19:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My April 15, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d351-f1"/> The Government newspaper
                    to-night says that Argentine Government sent peremptory instructions to the
                    Minister, Berlin, to demand apology for sinking brigantine besides money
                    indemnity, and anticipating Germany’s [refusal?] says that Argentina’s course is
                    clear.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
